# Safety Boundaries

These rules always apply.

Never create or modify live trading interfaces.

Never create or modify broker APIs.

Never create or modify automatic order placement logic.

Never create or modify OMS or EMS logic.

Never create or modify Portfolio Risk Brain logic.

Never create real account configuration files.

Never write API keys, tokens, passwords, or secrets.

Never commit .env files.

Never commit credentials.json.

Never commit secrets directories.

Never commit real data_store market data.

Never commit large licensed market data files.

Never add production credentials to docs, tests, configs, or source code.

If a task appears to require credentials, create a safe placeholder and document that real values must come from environment variables.

Default tests must not require real credentials.

Default tests must not make live network calls.
